usage: guarded_helper_close.py [-h] [--game-sdk GAME_SDK]
                               [--game-sdk-sha256 GAME_SDK_SHA256]
                               [--game-native GAME_NATIVE]
                               [--game-native-sha256 GAME_NATIVE_SHA256]
                               [--output OUTPUT] [--execute-root-authorized]
                               [--wait-seconds WAIT_SECONDS]
                               [--summary SUMMARY]
                               {check-source,check-game-exit,close-client,stop-keeper,release-screen}

R17 root-only post-game-exit close candidate. No SDK/game calls or PID reopen.
Without --execute-root-authorized this only validates existing facts. The root
must first complete B4/B5 and preserve the actual checkpoint. This program
never performs normal exit; it consumes the official original-HANDLE exit
receipt.

positional arguments:
  {check-source,check-game-exit,close-client,stop-keeper,release-screen}

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --game-sdk GAME_SDK
  --game-sdk-sha256 GAME_SDK_SHA256
  --game-native GAME_NATIVE
  --game-native-sha256 GAME_NATIVE_SHA256
  --output OUTPUT
  --execute-root-authorized
                        Only root may explicitly select this after actual
                        B5/checkpoint preservation; never sends normal-exit
                        tools
  --wait-seconds WAIT_SECONDS
  --summary SUMMARY
